{
  "schema_version": "0.1",
  "id": "streamsim/air-dryer",
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Heat-reactivated desiccant air dryer",
  "description": "Twin-tower desiccant dryer: the bed saturates with the moisture that passes, a timed regeneration removes it, and the pressure dew point follows the bed state and how much of the desiccant still works. A worn bed raises the dew point over days; a manual regeneration clears the saturation but cannot cure a worn bed, and costs heater power and purge air.",
